+**Publication law at C (source37 owner correction, A37-02).** The corrected DDL refuses every
+`grant_journal_v3` append while no format row exists, and couples `first_generation` to
+`migrated_from` (exactly 1 fresh, at least 2 migrated). Act C, fresh or resuming `{A, B}`, therefore
+verifies in the transaction that publishes the row: the seven definitions, an empty `grant_journal_v3`,
+and a surviving witness naming the admitted `projectKeyDigest`. A row or definition failure is
+`MIGRATION.CORRUPT`; a witness naming another project is a carrier project binding mismatch; either
+way nothing is published and no marker is written. Values are read under the held lease at C, never
+carried from the stopped attempt. Routes: `carrier-format.v3.md` §8.1.
+
